Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.98,0:00:05.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it? \NIt's the middle of the night.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.31,0:00:08.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, there's just something that was concerning me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.03,0:00:09.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If it's about Scar, \NI still don't have anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.87,0:00:12.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or is this about Marcoh, \Nin the care of the Führer?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.74,0:00:14.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, there is that too,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.41,0:00:17.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but lately, it feels like \Nwe haven't even appeared—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.64,0:00:21.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That idiot. \NHe doesn't know how I feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.79,0:00:26.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if you shouldn't have also reported to Colonel Mustang.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.81,0:00:29.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,About the brothers, I mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.18,0:00:32.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't need to tell him. \NNot yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.36,0:00:37.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The group that I was going to send to the library for security is standing by.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.22,0:00:40.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They should be more reliable than I am for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.43,0:00:41.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does that mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.52,0:00:45.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. On my own authority, \NI approve the entrance and investigation
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.21,0:00:47.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,of the site of the 5th Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.58,0:00:50.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, get ready to be punished.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.94,0:01:20.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hate that place!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.88,0:01:24.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been a long time, huh, boy?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.90,0:01:29.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, I guess it was \Nfour years ago that you first saw me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.31,0:01:32.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That night, \Nwith the pretty fireworks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.02,0:01:41.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who in the world are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.52,0:01:44.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That other guy said \Nyou were a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.39,0:01:46.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But that couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.08,0:01:48.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.68,0:01:53.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A homunculus is an \Nartificially created person.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.00,0:01:55.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A human who isn't human...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.06,0:02:02.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But there has never been anyone \Nwho could create one. It's impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.68,0:02:05.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Impossible? There's no such thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.95,0:02:10.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, there's a boy who is nothing but a soul standing in front of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.86,0:02:17.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not a person!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.06,0:02:23.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can I eat him?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.14,0:02:34.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.88,0:02:38.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.14,0:02:43.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.88,0:02:50.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.31,0:04:32.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm starting to understand \Nthe research that took place here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.22,0:04:36.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The gist of it is the large-scale military use of alchemy—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.50,0:04:40.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,in particular, research related to human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.88,0:04:45.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They used these incomplete Philosopher's Stones.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.37,0:04:50.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Knowing you, it's possible that you can complete the Philosopher's Stones.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.52,0:04:54.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know how these things are manufactured?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.48,0:04:58.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No. By the time \NI was brought here,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.11,0:05:01.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,those had already been mass-produced and then abandoned.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.39,0:05:06.71,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,The person who was in charge here before, \NDoctor Marcoh, must have left them behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.71,0:05:07.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.81,0:05:12.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Regardless of what they are made from, \Ndo they have any meaning?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.15,0:05:17.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if the ingredients are people,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.11,0:05:19.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,would you be able \Nto turn them back?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.80,0:05:30.14,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,In that case, making them into complete Stones would give them a lot more meaning.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.14,0:05:32.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I agree with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.58,0:05:33.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.64,0:05:38.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As they are, their lives \Nwill have meant nothing at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.15,0:05:39.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.80,0:05:48.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No meaning, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.02,0:06:00.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.58,0:06:04.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,your life hasn't lost its meaning, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.77,0:06:20.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You have overtime \Nthis late into the night?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.44,0:06:23.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,F-Führer! Sorry to cause a commotion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.51,0:06:27.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hear you have suspicions \Nabout the 5th Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.02,0:06:31.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There have been rumors before now, but I always overlooked them,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.25,0:06:35.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,thinking Brig. Gen. Grand was \Nworking for the good of the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.93,0:06:41.71,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,However, now that the lives of the two young alchemists are at stake, things are different.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.66,0:06:45.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll send a squad with the Major, \Nand go myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.86,0:06:48.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way \NI'm having you go in alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.76,0:06:54.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where is the scarred man?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.48,0:06:57.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He dropped into a nasty place.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.18,0:06:59.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see. No matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.25,0:07:03.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Greed may be coming to interfere.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.09,0:07:05.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll have to get the Fullmetal boy \Nto speed things up.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.18,0:07:17.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the area right above \Nthe transmutation circle, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.82,0:07:20.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They've been made into storage tanks, to supply the Philosopher's Stones
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.98,0:07:23.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,in the room below us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.20,0:07:30.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right, I can use this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.01,0:07:51.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You humans... Really, a hundred years can go by, and you never change.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.30,0:08:02.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's with that bastard?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.16,0:08:05.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is he really a soldier?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.04,0:08:12.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you still think that person is His Excellency, Basque Grand?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.27,0:08:16.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His Excellency isn't that great a bigwig.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.15,0:08:20.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to transmute in \Nboth rooms at the same time?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.43,0:08:25.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. The Philosopher's Stones in this room alone won't be enough,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.06,0:08:30.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and even Marcoh-san's research suggested a way of using two transmutation circles.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.84,0:08:34.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stones above, \Nand the Philosopher's Stones here,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.06,0:08:37.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,will collide with the two circles and condense together.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.26,0:08:40.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That kind of explosive power is necessary to refine them.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.45,0:08:42.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm changing the transmutation circle, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.24,0:08:54.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A transmutation circle with seven corners...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.34,0:08:55.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,First time I've seen one.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.95,0:08:57.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It just came to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.01,0:09:00.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I succeed in creating a Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.46,0:09:03.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to return Al to normal and then disappear.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.79,0:09:06.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can do whatever \Nyou want to after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.83,0:09:08.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm glad to hear that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.49,0:09:22.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let us out!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.58,0:09:24.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is anyone out there?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.28,0:09:25.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.50,0:09:27.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stifle it, will you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.54,0:09:30.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you all relaxed about?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.90,0:09:34.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not even you, the comrade-killer, \Nonce known as the Crimson Alchemist,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.51,0:09:36.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,can do anything about this, can you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.07,0:09:41.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know why I am \Ncalled the comrade-killer?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.90,0:09:45.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-You blew up all your comrades, right? \NWith bombs?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.51,0:09:46.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bombs?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.73,0:09:48.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have no need for such things.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.80,0:09:54.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The human body is \Ncomposed of mostly water,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.14,0:09:57.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but there is a certain quantity of metallic atoms included within.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.53,0:09:59.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By making use of that composition,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.42,0:10:02.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and a small amount of organic compounds,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.37,0:10:06.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can easily transmute \Nexplosive materials.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.69,0:10:11.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And... when surrounded \Nby this much red water,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.70,0:10:13.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,my power becomes...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.06,0:10:38.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are there people here?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.47,0:10:42.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Were there any other \Nresearchers left beside you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.48,0:10:46.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What those people are wearing are prisoner uniforms.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.32,0:10:55.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are they here?! If I had transmuted without knowing they were there...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.46,0:11:03.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys! Who brought you here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.51,0:11:07.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I did, Fullmetal Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.22,0:11:12.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Under my orders, the prisoners from the 2nd Prison were relocated here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.90,0:11:15.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And whose permission \Ndid {\i1}you{\i0} obtain to be here?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.54,0:11:21.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was a close one.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.25,0:11:25.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The general died, \Nright before my eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.27,0:11:30.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.44,0:11:32.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nice to meet you, \NFullmetal Pipsqueak.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.94,0:11:36.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm impressed that you found your way here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.50,0:11:39.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just kidding, you good-for-nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.51,0:11:45.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whoa! My, you really \Nare driven, huh, Pipsqeak?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.22,0:11:48.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's too bad. I really \Nhate fighting, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.32,0:11:50.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You shut up with that "Pipsqueak" stuff!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.15,0:11:52.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're the one who \Nstarted this fight!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.73,0:12:02.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good grief, you don't even know your own place.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.60,0:12:05.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know who you're \Npicking a fight with? Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.92,0:12:12.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've only kept you alive because we were told to keep you alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.20,0:12:15.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to pay...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.40,0:12:17.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're definitely going to pay!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.07,0:12:20.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You, who carry his blood!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.29,0:12:21.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Envy!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.51,0:12:27.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's your fault for not thoroughly checking the ingredients.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.15,0:12:30.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.78,0:12:34.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't want this experience to become any more painful, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.98,0:12:37.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If not, would you be good enough to continue with your transmutation for us?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.56,0:12:42.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've had a setback, but there are still ingredients remaining, and all...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.61,0:12:48.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Use these prisoners to create a Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.30,0:12:51.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You set this up for me to do from the start?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.21,0:13:01.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You aren't going to say no to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.42,0:13:05.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.93,0:13:08.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.84,0:13:11.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These guys... They're homunculi.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.75,0:13:14.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.36,0:13:16.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.86,0:13:26.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These people are all homunculi—\Nperfectly created humans.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.16,0:13:29.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They have promised to \Nreveal their secrets to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.87,0:13:32.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once they do, \NNina will come back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.31,0:13:37.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the point of bringing just her form back to life?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.10,0:13:40.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nina's spirit won't be in there!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.39,0:13:42.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I {\i1}do{\i0} have her spirit.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.75,0:13:43.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.86,0:13:47.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Nina that lives in my memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.90,0:13:52.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will transplant all of it \Ninto the homunculus Nina.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.13,0:13:54.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once I do, the truly perfect Nina—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.47,0:13:57.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the greatest one that \NI could desire—will be born.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.84,0:14:00.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Transplant... memories?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.23,0:14:02.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That won't be Nina!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.06,0:14:06.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, that's enough chit-chat.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.72,0:14:08.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal Pipsqueak,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.38,0:14:10.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,why don't you start the transmutation already?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.37,0:14:13.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,First, repair the ceiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.77,0:14:18.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.86,0:14:21.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We cannot use alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.10,0:14:24.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We have to ask \Nsomeone else to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.66,0:14:27.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't use alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.12,0:14:29.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then, why do you need the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.35,0:14:34.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you like Cornello?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.72,0:14:39.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you megalomaniacs, \Nwith designs on controlling the world?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.31,0:14:42.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We want to become human.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.63,0:14:45.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.97,0:14:51.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you really are homunculi,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.15,0:14:54.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then there must be \Nan alchemist who created you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.01,0:14:57.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And if even he couldn't create a Philosopher's Stone—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.01,0:15:00.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We weren't created by anyone! We were born!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.16,0:15:04.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All we can do...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.50,0:15:07.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is dangle hints about \Nthe Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.35,0:15:12.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,leading those who desire the Stone to someday complete it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.68,0:15:17.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on. Then you're the ones who taught Mugear how to use the red water?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.16,0:15:23.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And informed Marcoh-san and Tucker here in this laboratory of different things?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.06,0:15:27.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And in the town of Liore, gave Cornello that fake Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.69,0:15:32.07,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,By doing so, you fools who held interest in \Nthe Philosopher's Stone would gather around.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.77,0:15:36.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so, we found you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.43,0:15:41.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then I... ended up here?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.08,0:15:48.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No! Al and I came this far \Nfor our own sakes!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.24,0:15:52.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our long journey... \NWe've finally arrived...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.43,0:15:55.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because that's what we wanted.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.10,0:15:58.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We aren't being controlled by anyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.26,0:16:01.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's an equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.37,0:16:04.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We teach you the way to refine the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.74,0:16:06.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you use the Stone
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.93,0:16:09.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and turn us into humans.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.13,0:16:16.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't trust you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.14,0:16:18.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do not misunderstand.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.11,0:16:20.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We are not asking you to do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.88,0:16:25.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is an order.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.00,0:16:29.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all the trouble it took to bond this soul...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.01,0:16:31.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By doing this...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.07,0:16:37.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,H-Hey! Stop that! \NYou stupid bitch!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.79,0:16:41.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward Elric, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.23,0:16:58.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.23,0:16:59.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.51,0:17:03.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please stop! Please, don't do anything else to my brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.84,0:17:04.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.59,0:17:09.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, it's all right. \NAfter all, I'm just...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.16,0:17:11.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Suppose you were an imitation. What would you do then?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.35,0:17:14.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you have any proof that you ever really existed?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.84,0:17:17.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You keep quiet, Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.18,0:17:41.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, stop! Are you serious?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.02,0:17:54.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What folly! I knew I should have sent him back to God.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.94,0:17:57.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure the boy can do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.62,0:17:59.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.90,0:18:19.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, stop! \NThose people are human!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.73,0:18:22.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's right. So what?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.70,0:18:27.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want to go back to my original body if it means sacrificing other humans!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.51,0:18:31.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were aware of that from the beginning,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.35,0:18:33.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,when you tried to bring your mother back to life, weren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.04,0:18:39.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing else but a human life will do \Nwhen it comes to human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.57,0:18:46.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For someone to live, they must take from someone else's life, to some degree.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.17,0:18:51.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to accomplish something, a sacrifice must be made.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.24,0:18:53.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All grown-ups know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.26,0:18:54.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we didn't...!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.94,0:18:58.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You didn't care if you are cursed as dogs of the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.38,0:19:01.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what you decided when you entered adult society, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.61,0:19:04.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't go turning back into children, now that it suits you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.04,0:19:11.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So this is the truth behind truths, is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.84,0:19:18.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.80,0:19:20.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.62,0:19:23.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we give up here, \Nthen we'll never...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.41,0:19:42.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.45,0:19:46.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just can't...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.13,0:20:01.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.62,0:20:04.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Take your brother and go!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.43,0:20:06.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't be ridiculous!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.97,0:20:09.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The older brother \Nprotects the younger one!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.37,0:20:13.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.60,0:20:16.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We cannot allow \Nthis to end just yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.25,0:20:31.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, no...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.70,0:20:33.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even with the unfinished Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.87,0:20:37.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,with this much of it, \Nthe caster's power will be augmented.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.23,0:20:45.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ready to charge in \Nthrough the back entrance!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.51,0:20:47.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The surrounding area \Nis also sealed off!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.48,0:20:52.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I repeat, secure the large suit of armor and the boy with the braid.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.21,0:20:55.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Take anyone who appears to be \Na civilian employee into custody.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.73,0:20:57.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And everyone else?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.09,0:20:58.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mow them down!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.64,0:20:59.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Move in!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.19,0:21:07.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It couldn't be...! \NThe Crimson Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.05,0:21:25.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.83,0:21:28.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The transmutation reaction \Nis increasing without bound!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.96,0:21:30.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Ross!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.07,0:21:51.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.22,0:22:03.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good work.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.72,0:23:40.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.46,0:23:43.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 23: "Heart of Steel"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.52,0:23:49.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, what is it that you've been wanting to say for so long, but couldn't?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.40,0:23:53.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not, by any chance...?
